for your help Arm Pit Lumps: Causes & Treatment Tips Answered by Dr. Arvind Venkat on Nov 05, 2019 Lumps or masses under the arm (armpit) can be caused due to various reasons. Some common causes are as follows:
Cysts: These are fluid-filled sacs that may form under your arm. There are several types of cysts like simple cyst, lipoma, and ganglion cyst. Simple cyst is the most common type and usually goes away on its own without any treatment.
Fibroadenoma: This is a benign tumor found in breast tissue. It is very common in young women and often goes unnoticed unless it becomes large enough to cause discomfort or pain. Most fibroadenia are noncancerous (benign) but sometimes they can become cancerous over time if untreated. The lump may be firm, round, smooth, painless, mobile (can be moved), and not always located under arMPIT but can also appear close to breast area too. They require medical attention since removal may prevent potential problems down the road. Also, some lumps may actually represent enlarged lymph nodes from an infection or inflammation somewhere else in body. Therefore, it's crucial to get them checked out by doctor promptly so appropriate action can take place.
